  "behavioral_change": "numpy v_old 1.26.4 to v_new 2.0.2. Under NEP 50 weak scalar promotion (numpy.result_type, _set_promotion_state), xr.where(cond, float32_array, scalar) converts the scalar with asarray into a strong 0-d array, so the result silently becomes float64.",
  "downstream_effect": "No exception is raised; an assert dtype == float32 fails and the traceback does not enter the code that must be changed, which is inside duck_array_ops.",
  "reference_fix": "The reference fix changes the scalar handling inside duck_array_ops so that the result keeps float32.",
